  <h3>Project Identity in Docker</h3>
  <p>
    When multiple projects share the same <code>/workspace</code> mount path inside Docker containers,
    lean-ctx may confuse their data (graph index, semantic cache, etc.) because it uses the path to
    identify projects. To solve this, create a <code>.lean-ctx-id</code> file in your project root:
  </p>
  <pre><code># In your project root (before building the Docker image)
echo "my-unique-project-name" > .lean-ctx-id</code></pre>
  <p>
    This file takes highest priority for project identification — above git remote, package.json,
    and directory name. Include it in your <code>Dockerfile</code> or mount it as a volume.
    Existing data is automatically migrated from old hash directories when the identity changes.
  </p>

